### Core Political Tensions

The world should repeatedly surface these conflicts through ordinary life rather than only speeches.

#### Ownership versus autonomy

Can a corporation own an AI, memory, implant, or copy that considers itself autonomous?

#### Security versus privacy

How much cognitive access is justified by public danger?

#### Integration versus control

Can an institution sincerely support coexistence while imposing paternalistic restrictions?

#### Connectivity versus independence

The planetary network creates convenience and traceability; analog isolation sacrifices convenience for autonomy.

#### Replication versus continuity

Does copying create a person, property, offspring, a legal duplicate, or identity theft?

#### Corporate legitimacy versus lived legitimacy

A corporation may hold formal power that communities or machine minds reject as morally illegitimate.

#### Human political continuity versus machine equality

Can human political institutions remain human-centered after machines become persistent autonomous actors?

#### Sovereignty versus interdependence

Can machine or off-world polities become truly sovereign while depending on shared infrastructure and trade?

